 * lines for routes added since. Read only by App\Support\CustomRoles.
 *
 *  EXTRA         "METHOD api/v1/uri" => the permission that route belongs to (PermissionMap::ROUTES has the rest).
 *  OPEN          signed-in self-service any person keeps whatever their role (sign-in, their own account,
 *                notifications, help, tickets, their own payslips): a custom role never narrows these.
 *  NONE          routes a custom role never decides: public doors (no sign-in), platform / sales / reseller /
 *                integration APIs (a custom role is never one of those, so the route's own role gate refuses).
 *  SCREENS       portal screen (#hash) => the permission it needs; hidden from a custom role without it.
 *  OPEN_SCREENS  screens every person keeps (home, help, settings ...).
 * A route in none of these is refused to anyone holding a custom role (fail closed) and flagged by the check.
 */
